.TH AMBER-CLI 1 "October 2026" "amber" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amber-cli \- headless client for the amber AI agent harness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amber-cli
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIprompt\fR]
.br
.B amber-cli
.B update
[\fB\-\-print\fR]
.br
.B amber-cli
.B skills
\fIverb\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amber-cli
runs one agent turn without a terminal interface. The prompt is taken from
\fB\-\-prompt\fR, from the first positional argument, or from standard input;
the reply is written to standard output. Tool calls, approvals and the loop
behave exactly as in \fBamber\fR(1), so a scripted run and an interactive run
see the same harness.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-api\-base \fIurl\fR
OpenAI-compatible base URL (environment \fBAMBER_API_BASE\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-api\-key \fIkey\fR
API key (environment \fBAMBER_API_KEY\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-model \fIname\fR
Model name (environment \fBAMBER_MODEL\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-system \fIfile\fR
Markdown file holding the system prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-tools \fIfile\fR
Markdown file advertising the tool set.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIfile\fR
Read \fIKEY=VALUE\fR configuration from \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-prompt \fItext\fR
The user prompt. Without it, the prompt is read from standard input.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stream
Disable server-sent-event streaming.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-plugins
Run without the bundled plugins.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Auto-approve gated tools for this session.
.TP
.B \-\-yolo
Run every tool with no approval gate.
.TP
.B \-\-watch\-wake
After the turn, join running watches for up to 30 seconds and run one
follow-up turn with their reports.
.TP
.B \-\-mcp\-list
List the configured MCP prompt servers and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH THE UPDATE SUBCOMMAND
.B amber-cli update
never installs anything by itself. It detects the package manager for the
running system and either prints the exact command or, on an interactive
terminal after an explicit confirmation, runs it. It passes no
\fB\-\-yes\fR, runs no background check, and never writes outside the paths the
package manager owns.
.TP
.B \-\-print
Print the command that would run and exit 0, without asking. This is the form
to use from a script.
.PP
On Debian and Ubuntu the command is \fBapt-get update && apt-get install
\-\-only-upgrade\fR; on Fedora it is \fBdnf upgrade\fR. On macOS the command is
\fBbrew upgrade amber\fR, printed rather than run, because Homebrew owns that
prefix. Without a terminal and without \fB\-\-print\fR the command is printed and
the exit status is 2: nothing was performed.
.SH THE SKILLS SUBCOMMAND
.B amber-cli skills
finds, installs, updates and removes skills. Run \fBamber-cli skills\fR with no
verb for the verb list; \fB\-\-json\fR is accepted for machine-readable output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./amber.conf
Project configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amber/completions.json
The command tree.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amber/prompts/
System, tool, watch and domain prompts.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMBER_API_BASE, AMBER_API_KEY, AMBER_MODEL
Defaults for the matching flags.
.TP
.B AMBER_WORKSPACE
Workspace root the read and write tools are confined to.
.TP
.B AMBER_STREAM
Set to \fB0\fR to disable streaming.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a failed run, 2 when \fBupdate\fR declined to act because no
terminal was available.
.SH SECURITY
Without \fB\-\-yes\fR or \fB\-\-yolo\fR, a gated tool is denied when standard
input is not a terminal, so an unattended run fails closed rather than
executing commands nobody approved.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amber (1),
.BR amber-bench (1)
